Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Study Coach turns saved notes\Ninto explanations and practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.00,0:00:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the working Rust application,\Nwith a browser workspace.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Notes and history stay on this computer.\NAsking sends source text to a provider.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.00,0:00:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The comparison used the same 50 cases.\NEach new configuration ran once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.00,0:00:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The baseline scored 78%.\NThe revised prompt scored 86%.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.00,0:00:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Retrieval also scored 86%, using\N36.03% fewer mean input tokens.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.00,0:00:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Find the Test scope source\Nin the source panel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.00,0:00:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The source panel exposes the notes\Navailable for answering.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.00,0:00:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,An exact quotation must match\Nan original source passage.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.00,0:00:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring the original source passage\Ninto view before asking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.00,0:00:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Ask: How does a unit test differ\Nfrom an integration test?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.00,0:01:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This question uses the same\NRust core as the evaluator.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.00,0:01:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Ask Study Coach to send this question\Nto the selected Groq 120B model.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.00,0:01:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait for the provider response.\NThis is a real model request.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.00,0:01:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The response now includes an explanation\Nand source evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.00,0:01:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Read the explanation alongside\Nthe source quotation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.00,0:01:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The app checks that each quotation\Nappears in its named source.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.00,0:01:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,An exact quote is checkable evidence.\NIt does not prove every answer claim.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.00,0:01:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, test unclear input:\Nthree question marks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.00,0:01:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Try three question marks\Ninstead of a meaningful study question.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.00,0:01:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,An unclear question needs guidance\Nbefore a source based answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.00,0:01:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,For punctuation only input,\Na local clarification is enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.00,0:01:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The app asks for a clearer question.\NNo model request is needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.00,0:02:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Open My notes to add original material\Nto the local source library.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.00,0:02:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Give the new source a title\Nand paste the short test scope passage.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.00,0:02:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Save Demo notes to make this source\Navailable for the next question.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.00,0:02:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The saved source now has a stable ID\Nin the local library.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.00,0:02:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Open Past questions to revisit\Nan earlier accepted answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.00,0:02:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,History keeps the question, response,\Nand evidence on this computer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.00,0:02:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Choose the saved question\Nto restore its explanation and evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The saved answer returns without\Nanother model request.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.00,0:02:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Connections lets users choose a model\Nand enter their own provider keys.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.00,0:02:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The key fields stay blank on this screen.\NSaved keys are not returned here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.00,0:02:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Groq and NVIDIA offer limited free access.\NThere is no automatic paid fallback.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.00,0:02:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Return to Study to keep learning\Nfrom the saved notes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.00,0:03:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,One run on visible development cases.\NThese results do not measure learning.
